G622.b:
⟪ἀπ-όλλυμι⟫ and ⟪ἀπολλύω⟫,
[in LXX for ⁨אבד⁩, etc. (38 words in all)].
⟪1.⟫ Act.,
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪to destroy utterly⟫, ⟪destroy⟫, ⟪kill⟫: ⟦Mark 1:24|Mk 1:24⟧, ⟦Mark 9:22|9:22⟧, al.; τ. ψνχήν, ⟦Matthew 10:28|Mt 10:28⟧, al.;
	⟪(2)⟫ ⟪to lose utterly⟫: ⟦Matthew 10:42|Mt 10:42⟧, al.; metaph., of failing to save, ⟦John 6:39|Jo 6:39⟧ ⟦John 18:9|18:9⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Mid.,
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪to perish⟫;
		⟪(a)⟫ of things: ⟦Matthew 5:29|Mt 5:29⟧, ⟦John 6:12|Jo 6:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:11|He 1:11⟧(LXX), al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of persons: ⟦Matthew 8:26|Mt 8:26⟧, al. Metaph., of loss of eternal life, ⟦John 3:15|Jo 3:15⟧, ⟦John 3:16|16⟧ ⟦John 10:28|10:28⟧ ⟦John 17:12|17:12⟧, ⟦Romans 2:12|Ro 2:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 8:11|I Co 8:11⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 15:18|15:18⟧, ⟦2 Peter 3:9|II Pe 3:9⟧. In οἱ ἀπολλύμενοι, ⟪the perishing⟫, contrasted in ⟦1 Corinthians 1:18|I Co 1:18⟧, al., with οἱ σωζόμενοι, the "perfective" force of the verb, wh. "implies the completion of the process of destruction," is illustrated (v. M, Pr., 114 f.; M, Th., ii, 2:10);
	⟪(2)⟫ ⟪to be lost⟫: ⟦Luke 15:4|Lk 15:4⟧ ⟦Luke 21:18|21:18⟧. Metaph., on the basis of the relation between shepherd and flock, of spiritual destitution and alienation from God: ⟦Matthew 10:6|Mt 10:6⟧ ⟦Matthew 15:24|15:24⟧, ⟦Luke 19:10|Lk 19:10⟧ (MM, s.v.; DCG, i, 191 f., ii, 76, 554; Cremer, 451).

G649.b:
⟪ἀπο-στέλλω⟫,
[in LXX very freq., almost always for ⁨שׁלח⁩;] prop., ⟪to send away⟫, ⟪to dispatch⟫ on service;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to send⟫ with a commission, or on service;
	⟪(a)⟫ of persons: Christ, ⟦Matthew 10:40|Mt 10:40⟧; the apostles, ⟦Matthew 10:16|10:16⟧; servants, ⟦Mark 12:2|Mk 12:2⟧; angels, ⟦Mark 13:27|13:27⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of things: ὄνος, ⟦Matthew 21:3|Mt 21:3⟧; τὸ δρέπανον, ⟦Mark 4:29|Mk 4:29⟧; τ. λόγον, ⟦Acts 10:36|Ac 10:36⟧; τ. ἐπαγγελίαν (i.e. the promised Holy Spirit), ⟦Luke 24:49|Lk 24:49⟧, Rec.; seq. εἰς, ⟦Matthew 20:2|Mt 20:2⟧, ⟦Luke 11:49|Lk 11:49⟧, ⟦John 3:17|Jo 3:17⟧; ὀπίσω, ⟦Luke 19:14|Lk 19:14⟧; ἔμπροσθεν, ⟦John 3:28|Jo 3:28⟧; πρὸ προσώπου, ⟦Matthew 11:10|Mt 11:10⟧; πρός, ⟦Matthew 21:34|Mt 21:34⟧; with ref. to sender or place of departure: ἀπό, ⟦Luke 1:26|Lk 1:26⟧ (Rec. ὑπό); παρά, ⟦John 1:6|Jo 1:6⟧; ἐκ, ⟦John 1:19|Jo 1:19⟧; ὑπό, ⟦Acts 10:17|Ac 10:17⟧ (Rec. ἀπό); seq. inf., ⟦Mark 3:14|Mk 3:14⟧, al.; ἵνα, ⟦Mark 12:2|Mk 12:2⟧, al.; εἰς (of purpose), ⟦Hebrews 1:14|He 1:14⟧; without direct obj.: seq. πρός, ⟦John 5:33|Jo 5:33⟧; λέγων, ⟦John 11:3|Jo 11:3⟧; ἀποστείλας, c. indic., ⟦Matthew 2:16|Mt 2:16⟧, ⟦Acts 7:14|Ac 7:14⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:1|Re 1:1⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to send away⟫, ⟪dismiss⟫: ⟦Luke 4:18|Lk 4:18⟧, ⟦Mark 5:10|Mk 5:10⟧ ⟦Mark 8:26|8:26⟧ ⟦Mark 12:3|12:3⟧ (cf. ἐξ-, συν-αποστέλλω).
SYN.: πέμπω, the general term. ἀ. "suggests official or authoritative sending" (v. Thayer, s.v. πέμπω; Westc., Jo., 298; Epp. Jo., 125; Cremer, 529; MM, s.v.).

G694.b:
⟪ἀργύριον⟫, -ου, τό
(< ἄργυρος), [in LXX for ⁨כֶּסֶף⁩ (⟦Genesis 13:2|Ge 13:2⟧, al.), exc. ⟦Lamentations 4:1|La 4:1⟧ (⁨כֶּתֶם⁩);] prop., ⟪a piece of silver⟫ (Lft., Notes, 191); in NT,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪silver⟫: ⟦Acts 3:6|Ac 3:6⟧ ⟦Acts 7:16|7:16⟧ ⟦Acts 19:19|19:19⟧ ⟦Acts 20:33|20:33⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:12|I Co 3:12⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:18|I Pe 1:18⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪money⟫: ⟦Matthew 25:18|Mt 25:18⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:27|27⟧, ⟦Mark 14:11|Mk 14:11⟧, ⟦Luke 9:3|Lk 9:3⟧ ⟦Luke 19:15|19:15⟧, ⟦Luke 19:23|23⟧ ⟦Luke 22:5|22:5⟧, ⟦Acts 8:20|Ac 8:20⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪a silver coin⟫: pl., ⟦Matthew 26:15|Mt 26:15⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:3|27:3⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:5|5⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:6|6⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:9|9⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:12|28:12⟧, ⟦Matthew 28:15|15⟧, where the value is that of a shekel or tetradrachm; ἀργυρίου μυριάδες πέντε (prob. drachmas; MM, s.v.), ⟦Acts 19:19|Ac 19:19⟧.†
